From 5d59461f1d0542db3c39f4576e45e2dbd950d248 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: stephan-xyz <stephan@zehrer.xyz>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 15:57:54 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] irqchip: a GIC that names itself as its parent is still the
 root

The BCM2711 devicetree (Pi 4, Pi 400) gives the GIC-400 node the virtual
GIC maintenance interrupt, with the GIC itself as interrupt parent. The
chip then had a parent, the tree had no root, and no interrupt controller
was initialized: no timer interrupt, no serial interrupt, and no IPIs, so
the secondary CPUs stayed off. Drop a connection from a controller to
itself.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/dtb/irqchip.rs | 7 +++++++
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/dtb/irqchip.rs b/src/dtb/irqchip.rs
index f591df3b..f65e7e5e 100644
--- a/src/dtb/irqchip.rs
+++ b/src/dtb/irqchip.rs
@@ -173,6 +173,13 @@ impl IrqChipList {
                     }
                 }
 
+                // A GIC-400 that names itself as its interrupt parent (the
+                // BCM2711 devicetree lists the virtual GIC maintenance
+                // interrupt) is still the root controller: drop the
+                // connection to itself, or the tree has no root and no
+                // controller gets initialized.
+                item.parents.retain(|conn| conn.parent_phandle != phandle);
+
                 self.chips.push(item);
             }
         }
